<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia's Ecopetrol sees crude output rise in '97.</title>
<headline>Colombia's Ecopetrol sees crude output rise in '97.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's state-run oil company Ecopetrol said Monday oil production from fields it operates would rise to an average of 473,000 barrels per day in 1997, a 13.7 percent rise over current levels.</p>
<p>The increase will mean Colombia's average overall output, including oil produced by private companies in association with Ecopetrol, will hit 723,000 barrels per day compared to the current levels of 628,000 barrels per day, Ecopetrol said in a communique.</p>
</text>
